I Solitude\par
\par
As I grow older,\par
\par
I keep finding that the happiness I love and always seek is a life of solitude.\par
\par
By solitude,\par
\par
I do not mean shutting society out completely.\par
\par
I mean being glad to be alone, somewhere quiet enough to hear my own thoughts speak.\par
\par
Being around people is not so bad.\par
\par
But when people voice their opinions, the ego within me grows wild.\par
\par
It shows its ugly pride, born of ignorance.\par
\par
Perhaps it is my own ego, swinging its trunk and tusks, always looking for something to defeat.\par
\par
When the storm settles,\par
\par
it is I who must sit and mourn the shame it has left behind.\par
\par
So I would rather live in solitude.\par
\par
Besides being free from troubling noise,\par
\par
there is no one to light the fire of my ego and send it dancing until it burns me to ashes.\par
\par
This may sound as though I blame others too much.\par
\par
Still, it is the best thought I have for myself at this time.\par
\par
When I have built enough inner strength and understand enough of how the world works,\par
\par
perhaps I will turn toward society once more.\par
\par
Or perhaps it is society itself that is simply too loud?}